course: dictionary
lesson: 6533
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. Nettle can be a noun, a wild plant, or a verb, meaning to annoy someone a little. The words around it tell you which meaning to choose.
explain: «Stinging nettles have tiny hairs that inject a stinging liquid.» Stinging, hairs and leaves are the clues. Here nettle is the plant, the one that causes the sting.
explain: «Brush your leg against a nettle and you feel it at once.» Brush and leg tell you that you are touching a plant, so this is the noun. If someone says «Her silly joke nettled me», the clue is a person who is bothered, so this is the verb.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. If "a wild plant with stinging hairs" makes sense, you have the right meaning. If not, try "to annoy a little".
fact: A nettle is a wild plant with jagged leaves covered in tiny hairs.
fact: The tiny hairs push chemicals into your skin when they break, causing an itchy, burning rash.
fact: As a verb, nettle means to annoy someone a little.
fact: Nettle stings usually fade within a day; wash the area and try not to scratch.
fact: Stinging nettles grow in hedges, woods and waste ground in many countries, including the UK and Australia.
exercise: «Brush your leg against a nettle and you feel it at once.» In this sentence, what is a nettle? | *A wild plant with stinging hairs | A kind of soup | A type of butterfly | A small, sharp stone
exercise: Nadia says, «Her silly joke nettled me.» What does nettled mean here? | *Annoyed a little | Covered in an itchy rash | Lost in the woods | Stung by a plant
exercise: «Tiny hairs on stinging nettle leaves inject a liquid that stings and itches, so keep away and wear long trousers on overgrown paths.» What does the sentence advise? | Pick the leaves for soup | *Wear long trousers and keep away | Scratch the itchy bumps | Walk barefoot through the path
test: «Nettle hairs are tiny brittle needles that break and push chemicals into the skin.» What happens when the hairs break? | They turn into spines | They grow into a new plant | *They push chemicals into the skin | They make the leaves glow
test: «Plants change these parts for special jobs: a cactus turned its leaves into spines, and a nettle grows stinging hairs.» What job do the nettle's hairs do? | Curl around other plants | *Sting anything that touches them | Store food in swollen leaves | Keep the plant warm
exam: What does the phrase «grasp the nettle» mean? | *Deal with a problem bravely | Ask someone else to sting you | Pick nettles with bare hands | Run away from a problem
